## Why This Is Asked

This checks ability to design a small-to-medium risk migrations, focusing on data integrity, rollback safety, and CI integration in a beginner-friendly but realistic setting.

## Key Concepts

- Data integrity during migration
- Migration rollback and idempotence
- End-to-end risk assessment with real-world flows
- Test data generation and diffing
- CI gating and feature flags

## Code Example

```javascript
// Migration test scaffold
async function testMigrationShadow() {
  const before = dumpOld("users");
  await runMigrationShadow();
  const after = dumpNew("settings");
  return compareSnapshots(before, after);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test partial migrations and ensure no partial writes remain?
- How would you handle nested/optional user settings during schema evolution?
